# Netlify headers. Plain text, no build step required.

# CACHING — read before changing any max-age here.
#
# There is no build step and no filename hashing: this deploys by dragging
# the folder to Netlify Drop, so css/02-base.css keeps that exact URL
# forever. `immutable` tells a browser never to revalidate for the lifetime
# of the entry, so the year-long immutable values these rules used to carry
# meant returning visitors were pinned to whatever CSS/JS they first
# downloaded — no fix could reach them for up to a year.
#
# Worse than merely stale: caches expire per-file, so a visitor could hold
# old CSS while fetching new JS. The JS would then set classes and call
# APIs the cached CSS knows nothing about, which breaks the page in ways
# that are near-impossible to reproduce locally.
#
# So: revalidate HTML/CSS/JS every time (a 304 is a few hundred bytes),
# and give assets a week rather than a year, since CONTENT.md B2 requires
# swapping the placeholder photography in at these same filenames.
#
# If page weight ever justifies long caching again, add a hash or ?v= to
# the filenames FIRST, then restore immutable. Never immutable without it.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# CONTENT-SECURITY-POLICY — notes for the header at the bottom of this file.
#
# Worth writing now specifically because removing the Lenis CDN left this
# site with exactly two external origins, both Google Fonts — so the policy
# can be tight rather than a list of exceptions that defeats the point.
#
#   script-src 'self'      every script is a local file. No inline handlers
#                          anywhere, and the one inline <script> in <head>
#                          (adding the .js class) is allowed by hash rather
#                          than by 'unsafe-inline', which would hand back
#                          most of what CSP is for.
#
#                          ⚠ THE HASH IS OF THAT SCRIPT'S EXACT BYTES. Edit
#                          it — even the whitespace — and the browser blocks
#                          it. That fails safe (no .js class means content
#                          renders unanimated rather than invisible, and the
#                          hero renders open) but it fails silently, so
#                          recompute the hash if you touch that line:
#                            printf %s "SCRIPT_BODY" | openssl dgst -sha256 -binary | openssl base64
#
#   style-src              stylesheets are local; fonts.googleapis.com serves
#                          the @font-face CSS. 'unsafe-inline' is required
#                          because the page uses style="--i:N" attributes on
#                          gallery cells and CSP treats those as inline
#                          styles. It is a real weakening, but style-only:
#                          it cannot execute script.
#   font-src               the WOFF2s themselves come from gstatic.
#   img-src data:          the lightbox preloads Image() objects from
#                          same-origin paths; data: covers the inline SVG
#                          favicon.
#   frame-ancestors 'none' the modern X-Frame-Options, which stays below for
#                          older browsers that ignore this.
#   form-action 'none'     there is no form on this site. If one is ever
#                          added, this line must change or it will silently
#                          block the submit.
#
# Everything below must stay contiguous under /* — a blank line ends the
# block in Netlify's parser and would orphan the headers after it.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-/x7W7R75k8Roq0WaVRQX9blP4OufE5xbAdzklGxsgpw='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'
